        "epoch": 1,
        "hypothesis": "Replacing insertion sort's loop-carried shifts with qsort should avoid quadratic work for disordered buckets. After counting and prefixing, each bucket owns a disjoint index range, so sorting those ranges in parallel is race-free; bucket counting and scatter remain serial because their updates can collide.",
        "id": "811d3a8a4b024d5b",
        "ordinal": 1,
        "parent_id": null,
        "role": "B",
        "source_commits": [],
        "sources": [],
        "transformations": {
          "files": [
            "src/bucketsort.c"
          ],
          "retained": [
            "Count bucket sizes and use prefix offsets for correctly sized, disjoint storage instead of fixed equal-sized slices.",
            "Replace dependent insertion-sort shifts with qsort for each bucket.",
            "Parallelize independent bucket sorts with a dynamically scheduled OpenMP loop; leave potentially conflicting histogram and scatter updates serial."
          ]
        },
        "tree_id": "e1:B",
