    {
      "id": "452493e30fff45dd",
      "role": "B",
      "mission": {
        "base_commit": "0108834262345aef356edb6aa60f301dfc022408",
        "delegation_parent": "R/B",
        "depth": 2,
        "epoch": 1,
        "hypothesis": "The bucket-count and scatter passes have loop-carried dependencies because multiple elements may target the same bucket, so they cannot safely be marked SIMD. For sufficiently large inputs, per-thread histograms and cursors over disjoint input chunks can remove cross-thread conflicts while preserving exact bucket ranges; this may reduce serial preprocessing time before the existing parallel bucket sorts.",
        "id": "452493e30fff45dd",
        "ordinal": 2,
        "parent_id": "811d3a8a4b024d5b",
        "role": "B",
        "source_commits": [],
        "sources": [],
        "transformations": {
          "files": [
            "src/bucketsort.c"
          ],
          "retained": [
            "For large inputs in OpenMP builds, count bucket membership in per-thread histograms over balanced, disjoint input chunks.",
            "Prefix-sum each bucket's per-thread counts to assign exclusive scatter ranges, then scatter each chunk using its private cursors.",
            "Keep the existing serial path as a fallback and retain independent parallel sorting of disjoint bucket ranges."
          ]
        },
        "tree_id": "e1:B",
